# core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_bulk_f.tlk - bulk Surface push F: cheerful everyday small talk with
# the topic in the line (owner: TK; T5b). Clean in any room: no register word, no romance, no cool
# act, no guard change. Rule names end in _uf. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.

@rule core.small.uf1 act: backchannel
  "Oh, {x}. That's been on my mind lately too."
  "So {x} is the thing today. Fair enough."
  "{x:cap}, huh. I wasn't expecting that, but I like it."
  "Interesting. I had {x} on my list of things to think about."
@rule core.small.uf2 act: laugh
  "Ha! {x:cap} again? It's a good running joke by now."
  "Hee, I love how you bring up {x} every time."
  "Ha! {x:cap}. Somebody get me a snack for this conversation."
@rule core.small.uf3 act: joke
  "{x:cap}? I'd have a longer speech about it, but the snacks are calling."
  "If {x} were a snack, I'd have eaten it already. Several times."
  "Is {x} the new trend? I'll be the first to wear it badly."
@rule core.small.uf4 act: ask_about
  "Wait, tell me more about {x}. What's the best part?"
  "And what do you think of {x}, really? Be honest."
  "How did {x} start, anyway? Was there a moment?"
@rule core.small.uf5 act: tease
  "{x:cap}, huh? I think you've found a new favorite."
  "Still on {x}? I'm impressed, you've got stamina."
@rule core.small.uf6 act: agree
  "Yeah, {x} is pretty good. I'd say that to anyone."
  "Right, {x}. It's been on my list too."
@rule core.small.uf7 act: disagree
  "Hm, {x}? I'm not sure I'd go that far, honestly."
  "I see {x} differently, but I'm happy to hear your side."
@rule core.small.uf8 act: dismiss
  "Okay, we've done {x} to death. Next subject, please."
  "{x:cap} can have a day off from me, I think."
@rule core.small.uf9 act: complain
  "Ugh, {x} is so much hard work. Why is it always {x}?"
  "I'm sick of {x}. Give me something lighter, please."
@rule core.small.uf10 act: backchannel
  "Mm, {x}. Good, I'll keep it in mind."
  "Ah, {x}. Thanks for filling me in."
@rule core.small.uf11 act: answer
  "About {x}? I'd say it depends on how you look at it."
  "{x:cap}? It's pretty simple, once you get the hang of it."
@rule core.small.uf12 act: encourage
  "Go on, give {x} a try. I think you'll enjoy it."
  "You've got this with {x}. I'd bet on you."
